From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 04:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: nf_flow_table: remove hardware flows before
 unbinding

When a hardware offload flowtable is deleted, e.g. when the ruleset is
replaced, the commit unbinds the flowtable from its devices, which
removes the driver callbacks from its flow block, and the flowtable is
freed later.  Its flows are torn down then, but their hardware rules are
deleted through the callbacks of the block, which are gone: the driver
keeps the rules.

With mtk_eth_soc, the PPE keeps forwarding the flows past the new
ruleset, and after they end, until the entries age out.  The driver also
keeps its entries for the flows, keyed by the address of the flow tuple,
and a later flow allocated at the same address gets -EEXIST from it and
stays in software.

Remove the flows of a device from the hardware before unbinding it, as
nf_flow_table_indr_cleanup() does when an indirect block goes away, and
run the GC a second time after the offload work is flushed: the first
pass cannot queue the delete work of a flow whose add or stats work is
still pending.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
@@ -1331,6 +1331,19 @@ int nf_flow_table_offload_setup(struct n
 	if (!nf_flowtable_hw_offload(flowtable))
 		return nf_flow_offload_xdp_setup(flowtable, dev, cmd);
 
+	/* Hardware rules are deleted through the callbacks of the block:
+	 * delete those of the flows of the device before unbinding it.  A
+	 * flow whose offload work was pending in the first GC pass gets its
+	 * delete work in a second one.
+	 */
+	if (cmd == FLOW_BLOCK_UNBIND) {
+		nf_flow_table_gc_cleanup(flowtable, dev);
+		mod_delayed_work(system_power_efficient_wq,
+				 &flowtable->gc_work, 0);
+		flush_delayed_work(&flowtable->gc_work);
+		flush_workqueue(nf_flow_offload_del_wq);
+	}
+
 	if (dev->netdev_ops->ndo_setup_tc)
 		err = nf_flow_table_offload_cmd(&bo, flowtable, dev, cmd,
 						&extack);
